	)
	(text "Data straight from the Pico's USB test points TP3 (D+) / TP2 (D-) (U1, sheet 1), behind the 27R\nseries resistors on the Pico module. The Pico must be soldered FLAT on the board (castellated edge or\nthrough-hole pins, no header) so TP1-TP3 can be soldered from the back of the card.\nWith the Pico on headers or in a socket the TP pads do not reach the card: wire TP1-TP3 to the holes,\nor use a micro-USB OTG adapter on the Pico (with jumper J7) as on v1.3.0. Never use both at once.\nVBUS from ISA +5V via F1 (resettable, 0.5 A hold). The Pico VBUS pin is not used for this port.\nJ11 takes a USB-A OR a USB-C receptacle. R25/R26 (Rp 56k = default USB power) tell a USB-C\ndevice that this is a 5 V source; with a USB-A socket they are not connected (fit them anyway).\nUSB-C: VBUS is always on (no \"cold socket\"), so never connect J11 to another 5 V source (charger, PC).\nU12 (ESD array, SOT-23-6) is optional."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 63.5 134.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4008d3e9-a19e-5c0f-8563-5570f817a786")
	)
